description:
This is a perfect opportunity for your teen to learn the basics of hand building pottery, while having the support of our tutor. This will give them the introduction to explore clay and develop their own unique style.
Includes 5kg of clay and firing.
Number of classes: 5 weeks
Suitable for: Teens aged 13 - 18&nbsp;
Max people: 10
Tutor: Siriporn Falcon Grey &nbsp;&nbsp;

Join Frances to create your own rivers inspired miniature weaving. &nbsp;
Using a simple cardboard loom, this is your opportunity to try your hand at weaving using everyday materials and simple techniques.&nbsp;
All materials provided, suitable for adults and teens.

Celebrate NZ Music Month 2026 with a special cello and violin duo recital.
Featuring: 

Caleb Raymond (a 20 year-old cello performance student at the University of Auckland)&nbsp;
Melody Deverell (a talented 10 year-old violinist).

Both are part of West City String Orchestra and the Melody Quartet.&nbsp;
These two amazing and promising musicians will perform beautiful romantic pieces and are sure to inspire you.&nbsp;
